From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 10:52:52 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform-lynx

Atari Lynx gets its own shelf, Games/Lynx, for .lnx carts and headerless
.lyx images, on Beetle Lynx (Core::MednafenLynx, mednafen_lynx, option
prefix lynx) alone on a 240x160 canvas. Platform::Lynx is appended to
SHELVES and Core::MednafenLynx to EVERY; upstream's ALL lists stay as
they are and every policy question has an explicit Lynx answer: L and R
reach the game as Option 1 and 2, X and Y stay slot's, SELECT+X flips
the picture, rewind on, no core picker, no overscan, Stretch crops to
the 160x102 picture. slot_store::lynx reads the 64-byte LNX header
(LYNX, version 1): the title at 0x0a and the rotation byte at 0x3a; a
.lyx, a short file or another version falls back to the stem, and a
.lyx that is not 128, 256 or 512 KB is listed with a log line because
the core refuses it silently.

The Screen list gains Lynx, with Shader (Off, Grid, Dot and the retro
list, in Config/lynx_shader.txt) and Picture rows. Upstream test sites
(b), (e), (g) and (h) take the Lynx tokens. The cart is a placeholder
until the cards patch.

The shelf shape follows nelynes/slotPlus 749523c (GPL-3.0),
https://github.com/nelynes/slotPlus/commit/749523c
